{
 "$comment": "Where a hole lands, by holeLandings in streamlord-core Interpolation.kt, which interpolate calls, and by holes.ts in the VS Code analysis, both of which read these cases. Each %s in markup is a hole; position is the strictest of the three readings (HTML, svg or math, and svg or math with CDATA as text), attribute the quoted attribute it landed in, or null. HoleLandingsTest also holds every case to interpolate itself: a String is refused where the position refuses one, a Number where it refuses that. urls: whether the literal start of a URL attribute's value, prefix, already settles the scheme (urlSchemeFixedBy).",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "text",
   "markup": "<li>%s</li>",
   "landings": [
    {
     "position": "TEXT",
     "attribute": null
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "quoted attribute",
   "markup": "<li title=\"%s\">x</li>",
   "landings": [
